","s":{"2714457168":10,"3871231066":30,"4188031367":-20}},{"name":"Steady Rounds","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/6c6e1cc341487a8afd0b0c714a229255.png","desc":"This magazine is optimized for recoil control.\n  •  Greatly increases stability \n  •  Slightly decreases range\n  •  Increases airborne effectiveness","s":{"155624089":15,"1240592695":-5,"2714457168":7}},{"name":"Alloy Magazine","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/069170916c98748b7b3e33b80bd7d689.png","desc":"Faster reload when the magazine is nearly empty."},{"name":"Flared Magwell","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/f95e67e4ff37466505d66d3fa1030782.png","desc":"Optimized for fast reloading.\n  •  Slightly increases stability\n  •  Greatly increases reload speed","s":{"155624089":5,"4188031367":15}},{"name":"Ricochet Rounds","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/0a494d0442b32aff8c30d8b2b53561bd.png","desc":"Rounds ricochet off hard surfaces. \n  •  Increases stability \n  •  Slightly increases range","s":{"155624089":10,"1240592695":5}},{"name":"Light Mag","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/736b486ddb80beefacb4f09b5ad016eb.png","desc":"Improved reload and range.\n  •  Increases reload speed\n  •  Slightly increases range","s":{"1240592695":5,"4188031367":10}},{"name":"Armor-Piercing Rounds","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/b311ef00478243e21e2a5eec3a59f9d8.png","desc":"Rounds cause extra damage to combatants' shields and overpenetrate targets. \n  •  Slightly increases range","s":{"1240592695":5}},{"name":"Drop Mag","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/9d19f0c349652f0285bb5f999307b8a1.png","desc":"Increases reload speed but reduces magazine size.","s":{"4188031367":30}},{"name":"Assault Mag","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/953cfdeb2703978b1ab449b991b98989.png","desc":"This shotgun's magazine is optimized for quick combat.\n  •  Greatly increases stability\n  •  Increases rate of fire","s":{"155624089":15,"4284893193":10}},{"name":"High-Caliber Rounds","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/9d1c49edb2d2b24c74067742c09fd5a5.png","desc":"Shots from this weapon knock the target back farther.\n  •  Slightly increases range","s":{"1240592695":5}}]},{"label":"Trait","weight":3,"perks":[{"name":"Rapid Hit","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/de22847fa94634a487758041887bcdaa.png","desc":"Rapid precision hits temporarily increase stability and reload speed."},{"name":"No Distractions","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/3f6534e7fd934e0ecfeb1cac9da9c97f.png","desc":"Aiming this weapon for a short period reduces flinch."},{"name":"Subsistence","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/eaa8f4295a71bf47df7ffd8599f7af4d.png","desc":"Defeating targets partially reloads the magazine from reserves."},{"name":"Shoot to Loot","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/e8c6e23afe3c4215f0dc0c2941500c28.png","desc":"Shooting an Orb of Power picks it up. Shooting an ammo brick picks it up and automatically reloads all of your equipped weapons from reserves."},{"name":"Surplus","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/a4c054c3547840300b9ce7ef11b7b6fc.png","desc":"Increases handling, reload speed, and stability for each fully charged ability."},{"name":"Offhand Strike","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/599d73ea677633784655fc4161327c14.png","desc":"Final blows grant additional weapon range, stability, and accuracy when firing from the hip for a short duration."},{"name":"Moving Target","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/40b591eae7f122fdf1cfca21fc6f6c0f.png","desc":"Increased movement speed and target acquisition when moving while aiming down sights."},{"name":"Heating Up","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/39d2032b3c5bc7a5b2fe391c64ccb7db.png","desc":"Final blows with this weapon increase accuracy and stability while improving vertical recoil."},{"name":"Bottomless Grief","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/088930f7cf51b028acc8b7cb477fff9c.png","desc":"Increases magazine size. While you are the last living member of your fireteam, each final blow refills your magazine.","s":{"3871231066":30}}]},{"label":"Trait","weight":3,"perks":[{"name":"Frenzy","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/23e06f4ced1b3e6476f342978ff5bb37.png","desc":"Being in combat for an extended time increases damage, handling, and reload for this weapon until you are out of combat."},{"name":"Box Breathing","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/ef9c0dbddcb4c51fe5d3768e26b73746.png","desc":"Aiming this weapon for a short period without firing grants bonus range and precision damage that resets after firing or exiting zoom."},{"name":"Adagio","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/b344c34bf750a840b24ff5d2f8fe4507.png","desc":"After defeating a target, this weapon fires, charges, or draws more slowly and deals increased damage for a brief time."},{"name":"Gutshot Straight","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/5c4c785bde7b9808d48ded283256750e.png","desc":"Aiming down sights increases body shot damage, decreases target acquisition."},{"name":"Kinetic Tremors","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/300c343e6c33651a74d8a3fe81536146.png","desc":"Sustained kinetic damage to a target emits a shockwave that damages any nearby targets."},{"name":"Firefly","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/629e225e6f8214326bc1eb0a911a6f6d.png","desc":"Precision kills with this weapon increase reload speed and cause the target to explode, dealing Solar damage to nearby enemies."},{"name":"Adrenaline Junkie","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/6f8bde03140b53e6dc583ada1aeaa51d.png","desc":"This weapon gains increased damage and handling from final blows with grenades or this weapon."},{"name":"Explosive Payload","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/31f02e5f3bae68ecdfdd3f899cf931c7.png","desc":"Projectiles create an area-of-effect detonation on impact."},{"name":"Wellspring","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/ec2e3096ebd447bd6137735c9067b991.png","desc":"Kills with this weapon generate ability energy. This energy is divided between your uncharged abilities."},{"name":"One for All","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/b1bce269c3cd21393131b4f5cffae692.png","desc":"Hitting three separate targets increases damage for a moderate duration."},{"name":"High-Impact Reserves","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/33ed859a08f2ccf643a1ac3c7f201966.png","desc":"Rounds at the end of the magazine deal more damage."}]},{"label":"Origin Trait","weight":0.5,"perks":[{"name":"Stunning Recovery","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/0deaae9c67009f285a400ab5dd407138.png","desc":"Stunning a Champion refills your magazine, triggers health regeneration, and improves recovery for a short duration."},{"name":"Vanguard's Vindication","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/c7feebe5d55e4611c5d031d50eaca7ed.png","desc":"Final blows with this weapon grant a small amount of health."},{"name":"Omolon Fluid Dynamics","icon":"/common/destiny2_content/icons/e1d261e6c370349c7521ddda8fa70e78.png","desc":"This weapon has increased reload speed and stability for the top half of the magazine."}]}],"notes":["pandapaxxy (PvE / M+KB / Controller): Recommended MW: Reload. Precision(180) Kinetic Scout Rifle Primary Ammo. \"Hung Jury SR4 makes its fourth return. While I never got behind this weapon I am upset that Hung Jury SR4 has had three different versions in D2 and its original version in D1. Give me back the Black Armory weapons please and thank you. In terms of this new-new version of Hung Jury SR4 you will want Kinetic Tremors or Firefly for your AoE damage. Frenzy gives you some great damage coupled with any spec mod. Rapid Hit is a bit overkill for reload but gives decent stability. Arrowhead Brake brings up the recoil direction to 100 for an easy shooting experience.\"","pandapaxxy (PvP / Controller): Recommended MW: Stability. Precision(180) Kinetic Scout Rifle Primary Ammo. \"In PvP Hung jury SR4 has one niche and that is with Box Breathing. Three-taps with Box Breathing and Rapid Hit will be a super easy shooting experience. You might lane with this gun more than others but it will give you a blistering fast TtK. Think Not Forgotten and Luna’s Howl time to kill.\"","pandapaxxy (PvP / M+KB): Recommended MW: Range. Precision(180) Kinetic Scout Rifle Primary Ammo. \"In PvP Hung jury SR4 has one niche and that is with Box Breathing. Three-taps with Box Breathing and Rapid Hit will be a super easy shooting experience. You might lane with this gun more than others but it will give you a blistering fast TtK. Think Not Forgotten and Luna’s Howl time to kill.\"","pandapaxxy (PvE / M+KB / Controller): \"Does that make this version the best version yet? Kinda not really. All the base stats are the same The new Hung Jury now has the origin traits. It lost bottomless grief, one for all and adrenaline junkie. All fantastic perks depending on what you like to use. In their place we received no distractions, and frenzy. Frenzy is a fantastic addition and I love seeing it on more weapons, but losing things to not have as strong of a weapon next time around is a let down.\" Recommended MW - Reload.","pandapaxxy (PvP / M+KB): \"With the lower damage box breathing does and losing moving target I don’t think Hung Jury has much of a place in PvP.\" Recommended MW - Handling.","pandapaxxy (PvP / Controller): \"With the lower damage box breathing does and losing moving target I don’t think Hung Jury has much of a place in PvP.\" Recommended MW - Stability.","First choice PvP roll for duelling. Inspired by DMB Podcast 275 conversation with @DefyFly. The main draw for Hung Jury as at v6.2.0.6 is Box Breathing in the second trait column, which means you can three tap any resilience (2 Crit + 1 Body of a 0.67s TTK) and two tap tap lower resiliences, as at Season 18 v6.2.0.6. To proc it though, you need to almost treat the weapon like it needs pre-charging by ADS-ing before an ancounter, It goes without saying, you need to land crits and stay mobile. You don't need extra range, so focus on Handling and Stability with your barrel and mag. Rapid Hit in the first trait column helps further with Stability (as well as a Reload Speed boost) Recommended MW: Handling, with a Full Auto Retrofit mod, Radar Tuner (to help you stay aware of your surroundings if hardscoping), Quick Access Sling or Sprint Grip mod depending on your preference.","Inspired by DMB Podcast 275 conversation with @DefyFly. First choice PvP roll for duelling. The main draw for Hung Jury as at v6.2.0.6 is Box Breathing in the second trait column, which means you can three tap any resilience (2 Crit + 1 Body of a 0.67s TTK) and two tap tap lower resiliences, as at Season 18 v6.2.0.6. To proc it though, you need to almost treat the weapon like it needs pre-charging by ADS-ing before an ancounter, It goes without saying, you need to land crits and stay mobile. You don't need extra range, so focus on Handling and stability with your barrel and mag. Rapid Hit helps further with Stability (as well as a Reload Speed boost), Moving Target adds a little extra crit stickiness or Surplus adds gunfeel boosts, as long as you hang on to your abilities. Recommended MW: Handling, with a Full Auto Retrofit mod, Radar Tuner (to help you stay aware of your surroundings if hardscoping), Quick Access Sling or Sprint Grip mod depending on your preference.","[YeezyGT's S16] [MW: Any] \"Hung Jury is a fantastic option for high-end content, rivalled in-slot primarily by Night Watch. It really comes down to personal preference - in general, Explosive Rounds on a Scout Rifle is fantastic, Rapid Hit is fantastic, Subsistence is fantastic... Hung Jury's a great workhorse and it can't really steer you wrong. Even on the Adept, I appreciate having a few more bullets in the mag with Backup Mag as I've always been an Overflow Night Watch guy.\" tags:god-pve","Inspired by DMB Player Versus Enemies Podcast 2. PvE first choice roll for end game content. Rapid Hit more than offsets the Extended Barrel reload penalty, and Explosive Payload adds flinch and better anti-Overload Champion performance when that mod's in town. Recommended MW: Reload Speed or Stability, with Backup Mag or damage-boosting (Adept Big Ones, Minor, or Taken Spec) mod.","Inspired by DMB Player Versus Enemies Podcast 2. PvE first choice roll for non end game content. Recommended MW: Reload Speed or Stability, with Backup Mag or damage-boosting (Adept Big Ones, Minor, or Taken Spec) mod.","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 222. PvP/PvE first choice roll. Recommended MW: Stability with Adept Backup Mag (PvE) or Targeting Adjuster (PvP) mod. Good for Champion mods.","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 222. PvP first choice roll. Recommended MW: Stability with Targeting Adjuster mod.","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 222. PvP backup roll. Recommended MW: Stability with Targeting Adjuster mod.","Inspired by Destiny Massive Breakdowns Podcast 222. PvE first choice roll. Recommended MW: Stability with Adept Backup Mag mod.","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,god-pve)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,god-pvp)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: god-pvp)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,pve)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: controller,pvp)","File auto generated from csv pandapaxxy-s15-roundup (tags: pvp)","Chevy's S14 Super Pog PvE Loot List (MKB/PVE). Recommended MW - Reload/Handling","Diffizzle (PvE): B-Tier (Average). Recommended MW: Handling.","Diffizzle (PvP): B-Tier (Average). Recommended MW: Range."],"craftable":false,"sources":["Season of the Seraph Grandmaster Nightfall"],"activities":[],"hash":4074251943,"vendors":[],"frame":"Precision Frame","stats":{"list":[{"h":4284893193,"name":"Rounds Per Minute","max":100,"num":true,"interp":[[0,120],[20,150],[60,180],[80,200],[100,260]]},{"h":4043523819,"name":"Impact","max":100,"num":false,"interp":[[0,45],[20,60],[40